 "answer": "Based on the provided context, the promptfoo eval flag that runs each test case several times is `--repeat`. The `eval` command includes a parameter called `repeat`, which allows you to specify how many times each test should be run. For example, the command `promptfoo eval --repeat 3` will run the LLM three times for each test case, helping to gather a more comprehensive sample of how it performs at a given temperature.\n\nHere is the relevant excerpt from the context:\n\n```\nLLMs are inherently nondeterministic, which means their outputs will vary with each call at nonzero temperatures (and sometimes even at zero temperature).\n\nThe `eval` command has a parameter, `repeat`, which runs each test multiple times:\n\n```sh\npromptfoo eval --repeat 3\n```\n```\n\nTherefore, the flag to run each test case several times is `--repeat`.",
